Z||000012||mrfixit58||09-14-2000||02:43 PM||||Ricecooker,<P>yes, I've been to several games over the last 25 years. I can't say I made a regular thing out of it though. I really got tired of the Culverhouse family sucking the life out of the team. But, they are my hometown team so I've always looked forward toward better times. Now there here and I'm LOVIN'IT! <P>Frontal Lobe: yes the Silverdome is a tough place to play and the Bucs have always found interesting ways to lose up there. But the difference in this years team is the production on offence (so far). I'm not sold on Shaun King... yet. But Les Stecil(?) seems to bringing him along pretty well.<P>Regarding the old uniforms... there weren't too many jokes about them in the late seventies when the made it all the way to the NFC Championship game. All anyone ever talked about was the total domination of Lee Roy Selmon and the rest of the wreaking crew defence. Kind of like... NOW!<P>I, personally, don't care if they play in pink tutus (totos ??)... as long as they continue to win. But I do admit, I like the new uniforms better.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
