Z||000054||mrfixit58||10-04-2000||11:06 AM||||Well... it's Wednesday and I've just now cooled off enough to look at this thread. My worst fears are coming true... Shaun King is a rookie... and he's playing like it. He seems to have the talent but lacks consistancy. He throws a couple of very nice passes under pressure but misses the easy one on a critical down even when he has time.<P>I'm convinced that the offence will never be a real threat until the verticle passing game becomes a regular part of our offence. We need to try to hit Green more that once or twice a game, just to keep the safety's guessing.<P>Warrick Dunn is DONE. He was great in college because he played for a great team (FSU)in a weak conference (ACC - no offence ment, just a fact). We need a running back who won't go down when sneezed on.<P>Defence still looks good but seems to lack the quickness and pop that I saw last year. Still... way above average.<P>Monday night football is next. Culpepper, Moss, Carter, Smith, they are a real threat. Minnesota hasn't been killing everybody like last year. I'm hoping that Culpepper sees a lot of #99. The best way to defend against those big time recievers is to put and keep putting the QB on his back.<P>We're two games behind Minnasota already... we need to win this game... BAD!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||8
