Z||000060||RiceCooker||10-05-2000||02:32 PM||||I totally agree with you mrfixit58!<BR>Warrick Dunn had one good rookie season. Since then he has averaged about 3 yards per carry. Has anyone heard of Aaron Stecker? I didn't think so. How about Bears receiver Marcus Robinson? Yup. Last year he was NFL Europe's league MVP then came into the NFL and had an outstanding year and went to the Pro Bowl (i think). Aaron Stecker won NFL Europe's MVP honors this year and is currently backing up Warrick Dunn. He had another good preseason too. If Tony Dungy would start Stecker for one game, everyone would realize what the Bucs are lacking in the run game, a guy who can break the big run. The only reason i think Warrick is still in is cause he is great catching passes out of the backfield.<BR>Anyways, that's my long post for today<BR>Oh yeah, the bucs have only lost when i have missed the game but you better believe i'll be watchin it Monday night on mute.<BR>Does anyone here like Dennis Miller?||||reg||1
Z||000061||mrfixit58||10-05-2000||03:36 PM||||Dennis Miller is a DORK! I have a 4 year college degree and and don't understand what the heck he's talking about half the time. If MNF wanted to bring some comedy into booth, I think they should have a couple of fat guys in T-shirts swilling beer, burping and scratching. The conversation would go something like this...<P>" Hey Bubba (burp), can you believe that boy? If he don't ketch that there ball dim Bucs is gonna get a whuppin'. Hey, pass me them chips.<P>Yea, Virgil, and if'n that big white guy running wif da ball coughs it up one (burp) more time, I'm gonna send him a get well card... get well outa town, that is!"<P>Back to the game,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
