Z||000064||DJRice||10-09-2000||03:34 PM||||Playoffs one year, not jack the next.  The Jaguars loose again.  R.J. Soured (spelling error intentional) cant seem to catch the ball.  Whats left of the offensive line cant seem to pull its job off, and then in a brilliant move, one of the guys finishes out a play with a hook-uppercut combo so he can hit the showers early.  <B><I>But at least Jacksonville is ahead of Cincinatti in the AFC Central!</B></I>  Unfortunately, we will get smacked around again next week on MNF by the Titans.<P>Life cant be all bad...Miami is 5-1!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000065||RiceCooker||10-10-2000||02:41 PM||||That was a great Tussle, eh?<BR>Zach Weigert threw the left hook, right uppercut combo to perfection!<P>And the bucs lose again... sigh.<P>I'll tell you why they lost<BR>1: Three fumbles lost (giving up 17 points)<BR>2: Mike Alstott needs to work on his intermediate passing routes<BR>3: poor playcalling by Les Steckel. Yeah i know he's a smart guy and everything but there was no playaction last night!!! In short yardage & goalline situations, minnesota put eleven guys in the box. A little fake here or there would've easily got them a couple big plays.<BR>Anyways, i'm done crying for now.<BR>Me and my boys got two weeks to think about being 3-3.||||reg||1
Z||000066||mrfixit58||10-10-2000||05:30 PM||||You hit the nail on the head! I thought the play calling was great, EXCEPT, for short yardage. I can't see why, during short yardage situations, occationally why don't go with four wide-outs and a single back. This would force four defenders away from the box AND back the linebackers up to help double the middle and watch for the run. It may not work at the goal line but when your on the 50, why not? Everybody, including my 10 year old daughter knew Alstott was going to get the ball. That way the tight end was SOOOOO open. All Alstott had to do was put a little air under the ball and let hm run underneight it, then... touchdown. Good plan, poor execution. <P>Once again, Johnson had a chance to be a hero but he fumbled the ball then he dropped the pass at the five at the end. I'm beginning to think he's starting to think too much. It would help if King would quit throwing the ball behind him all the time.<P>It looked like the Vikes plan was to stuff the run, prevent the deep pass and make King throw underneigth the coverage to try and beat them. King almost pulled it off. Except for a couple of passes, he looked pretty good. I liked that 10 minute drive. Just needed seven at the end instead of three.<P>Oh well, we'll see them again in three weeks in Tampa. Did I mention I hate Moss?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000067||frontal lobe||10-12-2000||12:09 AM||||RiceCooker,<P>I kid you not, I thought of you when Alstott sailed that pass over the tight end's head.  What a GREAT call.<P>Poor Tony Dungy.  He seems like such a decent guy.  What must he have been thinking after that pass went SAILING over his head?  Those are like a punch in the gut.  Then you get to replay it in your head about a thousand times.||||reg||1
