Z||000111||RiceCooker||11-02-2000||07:07 PM||||Sorry "onfire" but the Chargers are due this weekend, and the seahawks are ripe for the taking. <BR>Don't get me wrong, the Seahawks will be a great team, but not for a couple years. It's because Mike Holmgren does not have a leader on his team. He builds a team the way he wants to and he gets rid of all the punks (guys who don't want to work hard). In Green Bay, Brett Favre was ready to break out and Holmgren and Favre fit together like the pieces of a puzzle. From there on. it was gravy.<BR>I think the Seahawks weren't as good last year as people think they were (remember the chargers had an 8-8 record!) Once a leader emerges and the younger players grow into Mike's style, the Seahawks will be a force to be reckoned with. <BR>They might get Drew Brees out of Purdue if they keep struggling. That would be sweet.||||reg||13
