Z||000138||frontal lobe||11-07-2000||05:27 PM||||Well, it usually draws a crowd of your teammates when an opposing player KICKS your teammate.  However, none of the Packers kept after him or hit him back.  So I would hardly call that taunting.<P>Being able to watch all the Packer-Viking games since Carter has been a Viking, he has ALWAYS acted like a complete jerk.  Maybe the rivalry brings out the worst in him and he only does it against Green Bay--that's usually the only time I see him play.<P>I got on the internet and read the column in the MINNESOTA paper by their columnist.  Even THEY said that Carter instigated it and the Packers got cheated.<P>Yes, Keyshawn Johnson would make most top 5 lists.||||reg||1
Z||000139||Black88GT||11-12-2000||04:32 PM||||<B>RAVENS DO THE IMPOSSIBLE!</B><P>What a game!  The Titans have a great team, but when the Ravens offense is playing good, they are very tough to beat, home or away.  The Titans have depended on E. George to get them out of jams, but it's not happening against the best run defense in the league.<P>To be honest with everyone, after Dilfer threw that interception I was ready to shoot him (as the rest of Baltimore), even though he had a great game otherwise.  Then he redeemed himself in the end, GOD I LOVE DILFER!<P>Del Greco could have been El Hero.  I feel bad for him though.  He will be hearing it for a long time to come.<P>Where are those Titan fans at?<P>  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<P>&lt;&lt;edited to take out broken links&gt;&gt;<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||6
