Z||000165||RiceCooker||11-25-2000||04:42 PM||||NFC PLAYOFF PICTURE<BR>-------------------<P>Who ever thought Philadelphia would be 10-6 this year!<BR>I thought they might have a shot at a wild card this year at 9-7 or 8-8 but consider this:<BR>They play Washington this weekend followed by Tennessee. After that they play Cleveland, then they get their bye week and finish the season off hosting the Bungles!<BR>New Orleans is on the way out. They have to play St. Louis twice and Denver.<BR>Detroit has a good record but they have yet to play Minnesota as well as travel to Green Bay and New York to play the Jets.<BR>A key wild card matchup is week 14 (next week) when Washington plays the Giants. Other than that, the Giants should cruise into the playoffs (unless they blow it) facing Arizona, Pittsburgh, Dallas & Jacksonville.<BR>Green Bay still has an outside shot at making the postseason as well but they are definitely going to play a spoiler role. They play Detroit in week 15, Minnesota in week 16, and Tampa in week 17.<P>My predictions: <P>Min: 12-4<BR>Stl: 12-4<BR>Was: 11-5<BR>TB : 11-5<BR>NYG: 10-6<BR>Phi: 10-6<BR>---------<BR>Det:  9-7<BR>GB :  8-8<BR>NWO:  8-8<P>Waddya Think?||||reg||4
Z||000166||Black88GT||11-26-2000||07:55 PM||||Rams lose?!?!?  WHAT THE HELL!!!<P>Saints are in first place without Williams OR Blake?!?  <P>Geesh, the surprises never end...<BR>well the bungles lost again, no surprise there...<P>Ravens let me down today, how did they let the Browns score on them?!<P>Exciting day in the NFL!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000167||ChadMan||11-27-2000||08:08 AM||||Yeah, Jeff, the Ravens are playing like the best team in the NFL right now, while the Browns are playing like the worst (doubt they could have beaten San Diego yesterday).<P>But I'm afraid you long-suffering Baltimore fans are in for more disappointment.  You see, Art Modell owns your team.  And as a long-time Browns fan, I can tell you a Modell-owned team will never win the Super Bowl.  When the Ravens stumble in the playoffs this January, he'll pick a scapegoat player and get rid of him (like he did Earnest Byner in Cleveland).  This will hurt the team's performance and alienate fans.  Then he'll alienate your great coach, who will leave for Kansas City.  Then he'll cut or trade more favorites (like he did Bernie Kosar).  Eventually he'll run the team into a mountain of debt and skip town.<P>Byner and Kosar went on to earn Super Bowl rings.  Modell doesn't have one, and never will.  That's justice for Modell, but I pity all you Baltimore fans who will have to wait for Modell to sell the team or drop dead before the Ravens win the Big One.<P>GO BROWNS! ||||reg||9
