Z||000222||ChadMan||12-28-2000||09:27 AM||||Wow, Bill.  No wonder you hate the Browns so much.  I'm sorry that happened to you.<P>Though I must say, it does take a strange mix of courage and foolishness to wear Bengals stuff into a mass of drunken louts like the Dawg Pound.<P>We had a few of those idiots at Ohio State, who would do things like egg the Michigan band bus and throw snowballs at Wolverine fans.  Like any Buckeye, I hate the Wolverines, but unless their fans are standing up taunting you in your own stadium, why not just leave 'em alone?||||reg||1
Z||000223||BENGAL4||12-28-2000||10:09 AM||||Chad,<P>I have attended Bengal road games in alot of cities. Cleveland is the only place where I had any trouble. Here they are in the order of hospitality.<P>1. NASHVILLE - The fans there are really glad you came.<P>2. MIAMI - I attended Super Bowl XXIII there. Had a great time. 49er fans were fun before and after the game.<P>3. KANSAS CITY - Rabid fans, but classy.<P>4. TAMPA BAY - Not too loud. I went there in 1990 when we were winning and they stunk. It's probably different know.<P>5. PITTSBURGH - Good time. Iv'e always respected the Steelers.<P>6. INDIANAPOLIS - They were obnoxious when they were losing.<P>7. BUFFALO - Almost as bad as Cleveland. When I was there, a few cars with Ohio plates, got their tires slashed.<P>8. CLEVELAND - As much as I dislike them, they are the best fans in football. They got hosed when Model took the Browns to <BR>Baltimore.<P>Jeff - As for what did I expect, Do you ever attend any games? If you do, then you know that all visiting teams have their rabid fans with them. Most of the Browns fans, respect someone that would go into enemy territory dressed like that. I am 6'1" and approx 270 lbs. Not many people are going to challenge me. This guy punched me in the back, with my back turned, standing at the urinal. Some one pointed him out, but he got <BR>away. I spend on an average, $3,000.00 a year, attending Bengal games. I have been there for the good times and the bad. When these playoff teams, start losing. We will see how many true fans there really are.<P>Bill<BR>86GT 3800 II S/C||||reg||10
