Z||000245||Black88GT||01-08-2001||03:17 PM||||You guys in Cleveland crack me up sometimes.  Modell wanted a new stadium, rightfully so considering he was playing in the worst field in football and the Indians got Jacobs field.  What did you expect Modell to do?  You guys picked him as a scapegoat, plain and simple.  In addition, you guys not only got a football team guaranteed afterwards, BUT you got to keep your name AND you got a new stadium.  <P>There is a forgotten story of the Baltimore Colts.  1983 Irsay SNUCK them out of town with no warnings, and we had no chance but to live with no team for 13 years.  We didn't get to keep our name or an immediate new stadium.  To add insult to injury, we were snubbed out of an Expansion team.  The Colts had just as much if not more history/legacy as the Cleveland Browns.  We had Unitas, we played in the "best game every played", and when it came down to it, we were crapped on by everyone in the NFL.  Admittedly, one of the main reasons was Jack Kent Cooke of the Redskins, but thats another story...<P>IMHO, you guys should be THANKING modell for leaving.  <P>We are lucky to have Billick.  He turned this team around in 2 seasons.  He should have been coach of the year.  Then for Tennessee to cry about the trash talking that was going on was sad.  Like Billick said, they did the same thing last year when they were underdogs going to Jacksonville.  Titans are just sore losers, after everyone in the media inflated their heads all week (well all season for that matter) only for them to lose to the lowly Ravens.... <P>  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 01-08-2001).]||||reg||1
