Z||000250||ChadMan||01-09-2001||08:48 AM||||I haven't forgotten the Colts, Jeff - that's why I'm happy for the fans of Baltimore.  But my distaste for Modell goes back to 1988, when he started dismantling the Super Bowl contending Browns.  Modell ordered the firing of Byner, wouldn't let Schottenheimer have total control of the offense and forced him out, then fumbled around with coaches Carson and Shofner until hiring Bill Belichick (who was hated by fans and players alike and will soon be fired by the Patriots), then allowed Belichick to screw over hometown hero Bernie Kosar...Browns fans hated Modell long before he moved the team to Baltimore.<P>You're right - Baltimore IS lucky to have Billick.  But if the Ravens come up just short, will Modell be able to keep his hands off and let Billick keep his defense intact and improve his offense so they can win the big one?  Or will he step in and start meddling, the way he did with Schottenheimer in 1988?<P>I realize I will be eating a lot of crow if the Ravens win it all this year.  But I don't think it's in the cards.<P>LOL at the "Del Flecto" and "Del Shanko" pics.||||reg||1
Z||000251||Black88GT||01-09-2001||09:07 AM||||Chad, I didn't know the situation in Cleveland.  Ironicly enough, the same situation is going on here, except in baseball, with Peter Angelos, the owner of the Orioles.  He is public enemy number 1 after he let Mussina go.  Everyone wants him to sell the team.<P>But anyway back to football.  Billick was the OC of the best offense in the league at that time, that was my point.  OK so they didn't win the Super Bowl, but the Vikings were awesome that year in offense.  It's OK Bengal, I would be mad to if I spent 3 grand a year to see a team painfully lose almost every game they play....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
