Z||000261||BENGAL4||01-10-2001||05:16 PM||||Jeff,<P>I don't think that spending alot of money on a team makes you a loyal fan. There are alot of ferverent fans that can't afford to go to the games. I happen to be blessed with a great career that alows me that luxury. Guessing that your around 18, I can see where your coming from. When I was 18, I worked at a grocery store, lived at home and spent every penny on my 69 Mach1. I not only love the Bengals but I love the whole NFL experience. Tailgaiting before and after the game. Going on road trips to see different teams and stadiums ect. GO RAIDERS.<P>Bill<P>P.S. If you think running up the score on an opponent is funny, then you have a much class as Billick. Which is none.||||reg||1
Z||000262||Black88GT||01-10-2001||08:58 PM||||Bengal, I must say you hit the nail on the head. I make dirt money, but what I do make, I spend on my Fiero.  Most of the time I go to the Ravens games because my uncle has season tickets and his wife doesn't always want to go.  I have only paid for the game once, and the tailgating beer was free.<P>I don't think Billick was running up the score.  I just think he wanted to run some new plays or get some new guys experience.  With the Ravens offense being so-so, we need all the experience we can get.<P>IMHO<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000263||mrfixit58||01-11-2001||10:02 AM||||OK. Now that my Bucs are out of it and the race for the Superbowl is down to four teams, here's my predictions:<P>Raiders over the Ravens. Why? because the Ravens look too much like the Bucs did in 1999 and the have Dilfer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> . All defense and NO offence. Unless their Special teams and Defense can score more points then their Offense, I don't think the Ravens can win. I think that the Raiders will shut down the Raven's running game and force Dilfer to throw picks. Still, I think the Ravens can keep it close if Dilfer throwns the ball less than 10 times. <P>Giants over Vikes. Why? because I HATE Randy Moss  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> . Really, this one is a closer call then the AFC game. Lots of intangables. But I think the Giants are capable of scoring a lot of points agains the weak defence of the Vikes. Shut down the big play and the Vikes can't win. I think the Giants have a good enough defence to do it. Good offense + good defense = Giants win.<P>So... Giants and Raiders in Tampa!<P>But, what do I know : rolleyes: ,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000264||RiceCooker||01-11-2001||11:46 AM||||I agree with your pics, Roy.<P>THEEEEEERRRRRAIIIIDDES are going to win because of attitude. Head coaching has a lot to do with it and Jon Gruden is one of the best - at coaching attitude. The Raiders will impose their will on the Ravens. (sorry Jeff)<P><BR>The Giants will win in a close game because of home field advantage and the Vikings one sidedness - if that's a word. The Vikes have offense. The Giants have offense (not as god as the Vikes') & defense.<P><BR>On an unrelated note, Michael Vick has now declared himself eligible for the NFL draft. The San Diego Chargers have just hired former Redskin coach Norv Turner as Offensive Coordinator. The players love their coach Mike Riley, even after a 1-15 season. The Chargers have first pick in the draft and are in desperate need of a quarterback. The Chargers also have some salary cap room. Corey Dillon, is available and has gained a lot more respect throughout the league this year as one of the best rushers. <BR>Now, I'm not saying all this is going to happen, but I do think that the Chargers will be the turnaround/surprise team of next year or the year after if they play their cards right. <BR>Junior Seau deserves it.||||reg||6
Z||000265||Black88GT||01-11-2001||11:48 AM||||Remember, the Raiders pass defense is ranked like 18th or 19th or something like that.  Dilfer might even have a good game against that.  The Ravens defense has carried them all season, and I don't see how its going to stop now.  The weak link before the last game of the year was Special Teams, now all of the sudden the special teams are playing great, couldn't have picked a better time.  <BR>  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000266||BENGAL4||01-11-2001||12:42 PM||||This weekend should be interesting. My heart wants the Raiders and the Vikings in the Bowl. My head says Ravens & Giants. Jeff, you are correct in stating that the Ravens special teams are coming on at the right time. When your offense is suspect, you need defense and ST to win. I have seen alot of the great defenses play,The Steel Curtain, the Vikings Purple Gang, the 85 Bears,the Giants with Lawrence Taylor, the current Bucs. I am choking as I say this, but the Ravens D has to be the best, with the Steel Curtain right there also. Defense wins championships and this might be Baltimore's year. I hope not. GO RAIDERS.<P>Bill<BR>86GT 3800 II S/C ||||reg||10
Z||000267||Black88GT||01-11-2001||01:05 PM||||Well I guess all thats left to be said about this weekend is, "we'll see"...<P>About Vick, I think he is being foolish for leaving early.  For one, he is almost a lock for the Heisman next year as long as he stays healthy, and while it might not be a big deal to him now, its always a nice award to add to your collection.  Secondly, I don't think he can cut it in the NFL.  His playing style is like that of Kordell Stewart, with the running/throwing doing it all type offense.  However, when he gets to the NFL where you have linebackers like Ray Lewis and Junior Seau, that will end real fast.  I don't think he has the experience for the NFL either.  He didn't play all of last season because of that ankle injury.  Oh well, it will be interesting to see how he does in San Diego (my prediction) where they already took one "questionable" QB out of the draft and look where that got them.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000268||RiceCooker||01-11-2001||01:24 PM||||Couldn't agree with you more on that one.<P>When he said he was going to stay, he was going to work on being a better pocket passer. And I thought, Wow this kid really is smart and knows what he's doing. His passing is great, but not by NFL standards. I only hope his learning curve is as good as his escapability. <BR>Remember, he did take the Hokies to the sugar bowl as a freshman.||||reg||1
Z||000269||mrfixit58||01-11-2001||04:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>OK. Now that my Bucs are out of it and the race for the Superbowl is down to four Ravens look too much like the Bucs did in teams, here's my predictions:<P>Raiders over the Ravens. Why? because the 1999 and the have Dilfer   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> . All defense and NO offence. Unless their Special teams and Defense can score more points then their Offense, I don't think the Ravens can win. I think that the Raiders will shut down the Raven's running game and force Dilfer to throw picks. Still, I think the Ravens can keep it close if Dilfer throwns the ball less than 10 times. <P>Giants over Vikes. Why? because I HATE Randy Moss   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> . Really, this one is a closer call then the AFC game. Lots of intangables. But I think the Giants are capable of scoring a lot of points agains the weak defence of the Vikes. Shut down the big play and the Vikes can't win. I think the Giants have a good enough defence to do it. Good offense + good defense = Giants win.<P>So... Giants and Raiders in Tampa!<P>But, what do I know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ,<BR>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000270||Black88GT||01-12-2001||08:28 PM||||Come on guys, just because your team is out of it doesn't mean you can't come back!!<P>We have to reach atleast 300 posts here.  Not sure what the record is, but that should smash it.<P>I was watching Inside the NFL again on HBO.  Marino kills me.  Last week, he said "whoever wins this game is going to the Super Bowl", becuase he was sooo sure that the Titans were going to win.  Now he says "is it ok if I take back would I said last week" what an idiot.  He couldn't take a team to the Super Bowl and he sure can't pick the teams going (ok I know that was a low blow) Then all the other guys agreed with him last week, and now they all turned and said that Oakland would wih.  Geesh!<BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
